  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $16.8B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency processed 24,320 awards with an average award size of $690K, and obligations fell 21.2% year over year. Annual obligations have trended down from $34.3B in FY21 through $16.8B in FY26. Computer and IT services lead spending by category, while biotechnology and pharmaceutical work also appear among the largest NAICS buckets. General Dynamics Information Technology, Inc. tops the vendor list with $753M, followed by Manhattan Torcon A Joint Venture at $492M and Deloitte Consulting LLP at $291M. The FY2026 to date totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date obligations rather than a full-year total. Contracting officers and program managers should note the concentration of dollars in Computer Systems Design Services at $2.6B and in several adjacent IT and consulting categories that together account for multiple billions. Health-oriented research and vaccine-related manufacturing also register among the top categories, indicating continued procurement across IT, scientific research, and medical product lines.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has HHS contract spending changed year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $16.8B in FY2026 to date, down 21.2% year over year. Obligations declined from $34.3B in FY21 to $16.8B in FY26, with the most recent full-year drop visible between FY25 at $21.3B and FY26 at $16.8B. The agency recorded 24,320 awards in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $690K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the largest contract categories and who wins the most work?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest NAICS category at $2.6B, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $1.4B and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $1.4B. Research and Development in Biotechnology is $1.2B and Custom Computer Programming Services is $1.1B, with additional spending in pharmaceuticals and construction. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. is the top vendor at $753M, followed by MANHATTAN TORCON A JOINT VENTURE at $492M and DELOITTE CONSULTING LLP at $291M."
      }
